One potentially meaningful optimization is CUDA Graph replay. The implementation has many separate launches around the big GEMMs; graph replay can remove steady-state Python/launch overhead if the evaluator reuses the same tensor addresses during timing. I’m adding a guarded graph cache and will test it immediately.
